cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Smart Road — automated Pavement Condition Index from road imagery
message: >-
  If you use this software, the trained weights or the dataset, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
type: software
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end implementation of ASTM D6433: road-surface distresses are
  detected in imagery, converted from pixels to square metres and metres on the
  road plane by inverse perspective mapping, and passed through the standard's
  deduct-value curves and corrected-deduct-value iteration to produce a Pavement
  Condition Index. The detector covers eight distress classes named and numbered
  to match the standard's catalogue, so detections feed the PCI calculation
  without a lossy mapping step. The PCI engine reproduces the worked example
  printed in ASTM D6433-07 (published max CDV 51 and PCI 49; this implementation
  gives 51.4 and 48.6) and is validated against a hand-measured field survey of
  1,810 m of Yangizamon street in Tashkent.

